# Codebase Engineer — frontend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the `frontend/` directory and fill in only the
# values you actually need. Every variable here is optional. Vite only
# exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to client code (see
# https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) — anything without that prefix
# is never bundled into the browser build. `.env` itself is gitignored, so
# nothing here gets committed.
#
# Unlike `backend/.env.example`, values set here are public: they end up in
# the JavaScript shipped to the browser. Never put secrets in a `VITE_`
# variable.

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on register/login) ---------------
#
# The public "site key" for the Turnstile widget the register/login forms
# render. Must match the widget whose secret key is set as
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY in backend/.env — see docs/AUTH.md. Leave unset to
# leave Turnstile off (the default).
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# --- API base URL ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not needed for normal development or the packaged app: the dev server
# proxies /api to the backend (see vite.config.ts), and the production
# build is served by the backend itself on the same origin (see
# docs/PACKAGING.md). Only set this if the frontend is deployed separately
# from the backend, on a different origin.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
